      "problem": "From the information given below, find all of the angles that are congruent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={30}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠B & ={150}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠C & ={180}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠D & ={180}^{∘}-m∠C, \\\\ m∠E & ={120}^{∘}+m∠A, \\\\ m∠F & =m∠E.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's find the measures of $∠D$, $∠E$ and $∠F:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠D & ={180}^{∘}-m∠C \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={0}^{∘} \\\\  \\\\ m∠E & ={120}^{∘}+m∠A \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={150}^{∘} \\\\  \\\\ m∠F & =m∠E={150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={30}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={150}^{∘} \\\\ m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={0}^{∘} \\\\ m∠E & ={150}^{∘} \\\\ m∠F & ={150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have that $m∠B=m∠E=m∠F.$ Therefore, $∠B≅∠E≅∠F.$",
